#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Theme</guilabel> tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A list of available themes is displayed on this tab. Select a theme by "
"clicking on an item in the list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the <guibutton>Get New Themes</guibutton> button to download additional "
"themes from the Internet or load a theme from file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Details</guilabel> tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A &kde; plasma desktop theme is made up of several components or items, "
"consisting mostly in svg backgrounds and colors schemes. This module allows "
"you to customize your desktop Plasma theme and to replace theme items with "
"items from other themes or from files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Desktop theme items consist in panel theme item, kickoff theme item, analog "
"clock, ..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to change your current theme for a full new theme (for example "
"from Breeze to Air) then you can do so in the <guilabel>Theme</guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All the available themes will be displayed on top, the current one being "
"highlighted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the list of items, for each item you would like to replace, select "
"replacement item from the drop list for that item. You may select the "
"corresponding item from another theme, or you may select a file. &plasma; "
"desktop theme items are svg files, except for the color scheme which is a "
"&kde; color scheme file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Customizing your plasma theme</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Customizing your plasma theme</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>Apply</guibutton> when all the changes have been made. This "
"will create a new theme named <guilabel>(Customized)</guilabel> and will "
"apply it to your desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The theme items listed are the most visible components of the plasma desktop "
"theme. Other theme components are not listed. Your newly created theme will "
"use these unlisted components from the theme that you selected at the start "
"of creating the customized theme."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "Naming a custom theme"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To provide a name for your customized theme, click on the <guilabel>More</"
"guilabel> checkbox and enter the name of the theme. You may also provide "
"your name (author), a theme version and a description of your theme. Click "
"<guibutton>Apply</guibutton> when done."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "Removing a theme"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the theme you would like to remove from the box above the list of "
"theme items. Click on the <guilabel>More</guilabel> check box. Click the "
"<guibutton>Remove Theme</guibutton> button to remove the selected theme."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>Exporting a theme to a file</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Exporting a theme to a file</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can share your newly customized theme with the community by exporting "
"the theme to a file. Select your customized theme from the box above the "
"list of theme items. Click on the <guilabel>More</guilabel> check box. Click "
"the <guibutton>Export Theme to File...</guibutton>. Enter the name of the "
"archiv file to which the theme will be saved."
msgstr ""
